  "help.quickstart": "Quick Start",
  "help.about": "About",
  "about.text": "A multilingual image analysis workbench for life-science research and teaching: image processing, selections and measurements, Western blot quantification, cell counting, fluorescence and colocalization, wound-healing assays, scripting and batch processing.",
  "about.libs": "Built with",
  "about.languages": "Languages",
  "help.html": "<h2>Quick start</h2><ol><li><b>Open an image</b> — <i>File ▸ Open</i>, drag files onto the window, or try <i>File ▸ Open Sample</i>.</li><li><b>Look around</b> — mouse wheel zooms, hold <b>Space</b> and drag to pan, <b>Ctrl+0</b> fits the window.</li><li><b>Select</b> — choose a tool on the left (rectangle, ellipse, polygon, freehand, line, points, wand) and draw. Drag inside a selection to move it, drag the handles to resize it, <b>Esc</b> clears it.</li><li><b>Measure</b> — <b>Ctrl+M</b> measures the selection (or the whole image). Use <b>Ctrl+T</b> to keep several selections in the ROI manager and measure them all.</li><li><b>Calibrate</b> — draw a line along a scale bar of known length, then <i>Image ▸ Set Scale</i>. All results are then reported in real units.</li><li><b>Analyze</b> — the tabs on the right hold the guided modules: Western blot, cell counting, fluorescence / colocalization and wound healing.</li><li><b>Export</b> — results appear at the bottom; <i>Export CSV</i> opens directly in Excel.</li><li><b>Automate</b> — every step is written to the <i>Recorder</i> tab. Paste it into <i>Analyze ▸ Batch Process Folder</i> to repeat the same analysis on a whole folder.</li></ol><h3>Good to know</h3><ul><li>Filters act inside the current area selection; without one they act on the whole image.</li><li><b>Ctrl+Z</b> undoes changes to pixel data.</li><li>Save as <b>TIFF</b> to keep bit depth, channels, stacks and calibration. PNG/JPEG save what you see.</li><li>Measurement column names (Area, Mean, IntDen, Circ. …) follow the ImageJ convention so that existing spreadsheets and scripts keep working.</li><li>To add a language, copy a file in the <code>locales</code> folder, translate the values, and restart.</li></ul>",
  "welcome.subtitle": "Open Research Image Studio — image analysis for the life sciences",
  "welcome.open": "Open Image…",
